@page "/docs/theming/tokens"

@* Exact values with CSS variables: the two levels, layers, light-dark() pairs, brand shades by
   hand, the surface ladder, theming part of a page, and the reference tables. From
   docs/styling.md ("Customizing", "Tokens", "Theming part of a page"). *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="tokens">
    <Lead>
        Everything the components draw comes from CSS variables starting <Code>--ib-</Code>. Set one in your own stylesheet
        for an exact value, on the whole app or on part of a page.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Two levels</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">IzzyTheme</Anchor> takes the choices that move many values together and keeps
            them right: contrast, light and dark pairs, whole pixels. A CSS variable takes one exact value:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@Root</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            IzzyBlazor's CSS sits in cascade layers (<Code>izzy.tokens</Code>, <Code>izzy.base</Code>,
            <Code>izzy.components</Code>, <Code>izzy.utilities</Code>), so a plain rule of yours wins, with no
            <Code>!important</Code> and no extra specificity.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Colors</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Colors are <Code>light-dark()</Code> pairs, so one value covers both schemes. Each accent, such as primary or
            danger, has an <Code>on-</Code> partner for text on it, and most a <Code>-text</Code> version for text on surfaces;
            change them together so contrast holds.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Add colors of your own the same way: define a new token such as <Code>--ib-color-promo</Code> and its
            <Code>--ib-color-on-promo</Code>, then use <Code>Color.Token("promo")</Code> or <Code>Accent.Token("promo")</Code>.
            Text on it takes the <Code>on-</Code> partner.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@OwnColor</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Brand shades by hand</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A <Code>Brand</Code> color sets four values, worked out for contrast. To choose them yourself, set the four
            tokens instead:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@BrandShades</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">The page and its surfaces</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Surfaces and overlays sit on the page; fills sit inside a surface and get stronger, from subtle to strong, by
            stepping away from it: darker in light mode, lighter in dark mode, where the page is the darkest layer.
        </TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Token</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Page</td><td><code>--ib-color-background</code></td><td>The page behind everything</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Surface</td><td><code>--ib-color-surface</code>, with a border</td><td>Cards, panels, tables, bars: anything on the page</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Overlay</td><td><code>--ib-color-surface-overlay</code>, with a shadow</td><td>Menus, popovers, dialogs, toasts</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Fills</td><td><code>--ib-color-fill-subtle</code></td><td>Large quiet fills inside a surface: a filled card, a panel, a band</td></tr>
                    <tr><td></td><td><code>--ib-color-fill</code></td><td>Small fills that must show: table heads, code, wells</td></tr>
                    <tr><td></td><td><code>--ib-color-fill-strong</code></td><td>Selected and pressed fills, chips, tracks, skeletons</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>
        <TextBlock>
            A fill straight on the page reads as a hole, not a card; put a surface between them. For a white page,
            set <Code>--ib-color-background</Code> to the surface color.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Theme part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Wrap the part in an <Code>IzzyTheme</Code>. It themes what's inside, and what it doesn't set comes from the theme
            around it.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="izzy-theme-part" />
        <TextBlock>
            It takes <Code>Brand</Code>, a built-in <Code>Gray</Code>, <Code>Radius</Code>, <Code>Density</Code>,
            <Code>Preset</Code> and <Code>ColorScheme</Code>, and renders a <Code>div</Code>. On part of a page a preset
            changes density, shape and the card shadow only. For one exact value, use <Code>Style</Code> or a class:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Part</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Colors made from the part's own, such as the focus ring, selected rows, hover washes and scrollbars, are worked
            out where they're used, so they follow it. So does a plain CSS rule on the part. In plain HTML,
            <Code>data-ib-brand</Code>, <Code>data-ib-gray</Code>, <Code>data-ib-radius</Code>, <Code>data-ib-density</Code>
            and <Code>data-ib-preset</Code> do the same on any element.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Menus, popovers, tooltips and a <Code>Dialog</Code> written in the page stay inside the part, so they take its
            theme. A dialog opened from code with <Code>DialogService</Code> doesn't: pass <Code>ColorScheme</Code>,
            <Code>Brand</Code> and <Code>Density</Code> in its <Code>DialogOptions</Code> to match. Its gray and radius stay
            the app's.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Every token</Heading>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Tokens</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Page and surfaces</td><td><code>--ib-color-background</code>, <code>-surface</code>, <code>-surface-overlay</code>, <code>-overlay-border</code> (an overlay's edge in dark mode), <code>-fill-subtle</code>, <code>-fill</code>, <code>-fill-strong</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Text and lines</td><td><code>--ib-color-on-surface</code>, <code>-muted</code>, <code>-subtle</code>, <code>-disabled</code>, <code>-border</code>, <code>-outline</code>, <code>-backdrop</code> (behind dialogs)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Brand</td><td><code>--ib-color-primary</code>, <code>-on-primary</code>, <code>-primary-text</code>, <code>-primary-soft</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Status</td><td><code>--ib-color-success</code>, <code>-warning</code>, <code>-danger</code>, <code>-info</code>, <code>-neutral</code>, each with <code>-on-</code>; the first four with <code>-text</code> and <code>-soft</code>. Tuned against every gray, so change them as a set.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Made from other colors</td><td><code>--ib-color-focus</code>, <code>--ib-color-halo</code>, <code>--ib-color-selected</code>, <code>--ib-state-hover</code>, <code>--ib-state-pressed</code>, <code>--ib-color-segment</code>, <code>--ib-color-on-segment</code>, <code>-segment-edge</code>, <code>-segment-track</code>, <code>--ib-color-scrollbar</code>, <code>-scrollbar-hover</code>. Unset: each is worked out where it's used; set one to replace that.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Shape</td><td><code>--ib-radius-none</code>, <code>-sm</code>, <code>-md</code>, <code>-lg</code>, <code>-xl</code>, <code>-full</code>; <code>--ib-radius-control</code> (buttons, fields, tags) and <code>--ib-radius-control-sm</code> (badges)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Density</td><td><code>--ib-control-h-sm</code>, <code>-md</code>, <code>-lg</code>; <code>--ib-control-font-sm</code>; <code>--ib-control-icon-sm</code>, <code>-md</code>, <code>-lg</code>; <code>--ib-table-cell-py</code>, <code>--ib-card-padding</code>; the spacing scale <code>--ib-space-0</code> to <code>-16</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Sizes</td><td><code>--ib-size-sm</code>, <code>-md</code>, <code>-lg</code>, <code>-xl</code> (640 to 1280px), <code>--ib-size-prose</code> (a readable line)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>--ib-font-body</code>, <code>-heading</code>, <code>-mono</code>; <code>--ib-text-xs</code> to <code>-6xl</code>; <code>--ib-weight-light</code> to <code>-extrabold</code>, and <code>-heading</code>; <code>--ib-leading-none</code> to <code>-loose</code>; <code>--ib-tracking-tighter</code> to <code>-widest</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Depth</td><td><code>--ib-shadow-none</code>, <code>-xs</code> (under cards), <code>-sm</code>, <code>-md</code>, <code>-lg</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Motion</td><td><code>--ib-duration-fast</code>, <code>--ib-duration-normal</code>, <code>--ib-ease</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Code</td><td><code>--ib-code-comment</code>, <code>-keyword</code>, <code>-string</code>, <code>-number</code>, <code>-type</code>, <code>-function</code>, <code>-tag</code>, <code>-attr</code>, <code>-meta</code>, each at least 4.5:1 on the code block</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>

        <Heading Level="2">Component variables</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A few components have their own variables for what people tune most. Anything not listed, including the
            <Code>.ib-*</Code> class names, is internal and may change; to style your own way, add a class with
            <Code>Class</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Variables</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Button, IconButton</td><td><code>--ib-btn-px</code> (side padding; Button only), <code>--ib-btn-radius</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Fields</td><td><code>--ib-field-radius</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>FileUpload</td><td><code>--ib-upload-bg</code>, <code>--ib-upload-border-color</code>, <code>--ib-upload-border-style</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Card</td><td><code>--ib-card-padding</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Table</td><td><code>--ib-table-cell-py</code>, <code>--ib-table-cell-px</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>AppShell</td><td><code>--ib-shell-{header,sidebar,main,aside,footer}-bg</code> and <code>-fg</code>, <code>--ib-shell-divider</code>, <code>--ib-shell-header-h</code>, <code>--ib-shell-footer-h</code>, <code>--ib-banner-h</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Icon</td><td><code>--ib-icon-stroke</code>, <code>--ib-spin-duration</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>AvatarGroup</td><td><code>--ib-avatar-ring</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Timeline</td><td><code>--ib-timeline-bg</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">Themes and presets</Anchor>: the choices <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> keeps right for you.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/color-scheme">Light and dark</Anchor>: the default scheme and a scheme for part of a page.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Root = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-focus: #7c3aed;     /* the focus ring and field halo */
          --ib-card-padding: 1.5rem;
          --ib-radius-xl: 0.5rem;        /* cards and other large panels */
        }
        """;

    private const string OwnColor = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-promo: light-dark(#7c3aed, #a78bfa);
          --ib-color-on-promo: light-dark(#ffffff, #1e1b4b);
        }
        """;

    private const string BrandShades = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-primary: light-dark(#0f766e, #2dd4bf);
          --ib-color-on-primary: light-dark(#ffffff, #042f2e);
          --ib-color-primary-text: light-dark(#115e59, #5eead4);  /* text on surfaces */
